From 6e791e28d5f0668fac662135f5b810f82d4a0da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auditor <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] main: a live-armed process must pass the promotion gate
 and attach the cleared signal

INVARIANT PROTECTED: no unmeasured strategy can touch real money, and the
promotion gate is consulted in code, not only in tools.

Finding (audit S20, the CRITICAL item): promotion_gate_allows_live() was
read only by tools/sliceNN_promotion_gate.py. Setting USE_TESTNET=0,
PAPER_TRADING=0, LIVE_TRADING_ACK=I_UNDERSTAND plus credentials on this
tree started the bot on mainnet with MarketStrategy (RSI/MACD/BB/
Supertrend voter, never scored against a null) at 0.5% risk, 2% notional
per trade, up to 3 positions, no $100 cap, and no reference to the
Stage-1 clear. Every documented fail-closed promotion invariant lived in
prose and in a report generator.

Thought process: config.py must stay the single authority on ARMING the
process (four-part chain, no FORCE_LIVE, AST-tested). The gate answers a
different question - has the STRATEGY earned live - so the check belongs
in the orchestrator, after assert_sandbox and before the first network
call, and it may only refuse. It is evaluated only when live is armed,
so paper/testnet behaviour is byte-identical (test pins that the gate is
never even imported in sandbox).

What changed:
  main.py            - TradingBot.live_promotion_check(): requires
                       promotion_gate_allows_live(config=cfg) AND
                       strategy.signal_name == ProjectStatus.cleared_edge_signal
                       (or no strategy). Exceptions refuse. startup() calls it
                       when live_armed and returns False on refusal.
  shadow_strategy.py - ShadowStrategy.signal_name = shadow.SHADOW_SIGNAL, the
                       only strategy class that carries the cleared identity.
  tests/test_live_promotion_check.py - 7 tests: refuses before any transport
                       request; names the gate; unnamed strategy refused even
                       with gate True; named+cleared+gate True passes; gate
                       exception refuses; sandbox never consults the gate.

What did NOT change: GATE_PATH, FUND_ABS, any threshold, config.py.
On this tree the check always refuses (2/8 items complete) - which is
the point: live is now impossible from this tree for the right reason.

Verification: 425 passed across orchestrator, paper cert, shadow pack,
config and the new file.

Revision after the full suite: tests/test_funding_carry_fade_btc_v1.py
::test_no_trading_path_consults_the_cleared_edge_field pins that main,
config, risk_management, trading_engine, position_sizing and policy never
contain the string cleared_edge_signal - "a research record would have
become a trading permission". The first cut of this patch read the field
in main.py to REFUSE, which is the opposite of a permission, but the
string guard is right in spirit and was not weakened. The comparison
now lives in promotion_gate.strategy_is_the_cleared_signal(): a
negative-only predicate (None strategy ok; no signal_name -> refuse;
mismatch -> refuse; a True is one necessary condition, never a grant).
main.py calls it and contains no reference to the research field. Two
tests added: main's source is clean of the string; the identity check
returning True still leaves promotion_gate_allows_live() False on this
tree. 9 tests in the file.
